Module gaunt "A Winter in Carth" {
  // ── The account ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At six on Ash Day the book closes on an account: each strand's morning after, told plainly, then one ending, by what
  // the Consistory did. No custom, no ever-after; the next morning, and stop.
  Rule fate_carth_released when accounting() and vigilReleased(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "At Carth there is a fire on the hearth and a cart of oak in the yard, and the forty nights are paid in full by the man who bought them, and the rent with them. Ralph Scaife is still in the byre, because the ground is still iron; but there is a lamp by him now, and nobody has to lie down with him to keep him warm." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_paid when accounting() and vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and scaifesPaid(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil was broken, and paid for in full all the same by the man who bought it, with a cart of oak besides; and the Scaifes owe nothing to anyone, which Will Scaife says he does not know how to feel about, and sits by his fire feeling it." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_forgiven when accounting() and vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and arrearsForgiven(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil was broken, and the Scaifes owe the Penitentiary twenty shillings they have not got; but the Fabric has forgiven them two years' rent, for reasons the Master of the Fabric describes as charity, and they keep the farm, and a fire, and the debt, which in Gaunt is the same as owning a cow." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_ruined when accounting() and vigilBroken(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil was broken, and the Scaifes owe the twenty shillings back, and the rent besides. At Lady Day the Fabric will have them off the fell. Annis Scaife has already been down to the Stand to ask the rates for a fast." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_kept_forgiven when accounting() and vigilOn() and arrearsForgiven(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil goes on, a night at a time, and Raistrick comes at three to put his hand in the ash. The Fabric has forgiven the arrears, so the Scaifes will be paid forty shillings for nothing they owe, at the thaw, and do not know what to do with that either." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Rule fate_carth_kept when accounting() and vigilOn() and not spread(fate_carth) says "The Carth vigil goes on: night twenty-six tonight, fourteen to go. Raistrick will come at three and kneel and put his hand in the ash, and say 'Kept', and go. At the thaw the Scaifes will be paid, and pay the Fabric, and be square, and it will be spring." { Assert spread(fate_carth). }
  Entity fate_carth: fact "Carth".
  Rule fate_child_dead when accounting() and dowsieDead(dowsie) and not spread(fate_child) says "Dowsie Scaife lies in the byre at Carth beside her grandfather, under a clean sheet, until the ground will take a spade." { Assert spread(fate_child). }
  Rule fate_child when accounting() and not dowsieDead(dowsie) and stayingAtCarth(party) and not spread(fate_child) says "Dowsie Scaife is up and about in her mother's shawl, with a cough she is proud of, telling the hens about the stone man in the Minster, who she has never seen." { Assert spread(fate_child). }
  Entity fate_child: fact "Dowsie".
  Rule fate_granny_dead when accounting() and grannyDead(granny) and not spread(fate_granny) says "Old Mother Scaife was found in the byre on the twenty-sixth morning of the vigil, under the sheet, with her arms round her husband, keeping him warm. There are two hurdles now." { Assert spread(fate_granny). }
  Rule fate_granny_laid when accounting() and ralphLaid(carth_vigil) and not grannyDead(granny) and not spread(fate_granny) says "Old Mother Scaife sits by the hearth at Carth in the rocking-chair and does not go into the byre at night. Ralph, she tells the hens, is going; he always was slow." { Assert spread(fate_granny). }
  Entity fate_granny: fact "the old woman".
  Rule fate_thackray_bore_warm when accounting() and thackrayBears(thackray) and vigilReleased(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_thackray) says "Hugh Thackray is struck from the Register of Gaunt and from the Ladder of Merit, where a mason has chiselled his name out of the gold, leaving a long pale scar at the top of the board that nobody will paint over. He walked to Carth in a pair of borrowed boots and knocked, and Annis Scaife let him in, and gave him the axe, and he is splitting the oak he sent up the fell, very badly, in the yard, in the snow, and will not come in to the fire until it is all done." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Rule fate_thackray_bore when accounting() and thackrayBears(thackray) and not spread(fate_thackray) says "Hugh Thackray is struck from the Register of Gaunt and from the Ladder of Merit, where a mason has chiselled his name out of the gold, leaving a long pale scar at the top of the board that nobody will paint over. He walked to Carth in a pair of borrowed boots and knocked, and Annis Scaife let him in, and he is sitting at a cold hearth he paid for, keeping the last of his own forty nights himself." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Rule fate_thackray_changed when accounting() and thackrayChanged() and not spread(fate_thackray) says "Alderman Thackray is still top of the Ladder, and cannot be got off it, because the Wood Exchange has given away more this week than the Ladder can count. Oak is twenty shillings the cord and the Row has the dead-wood right again. He looks ten years older and sleeps at night." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Rule fate_thackray_known when accounting() and knows(party, thackray_vigil) and not spread(fate_thackray) says "Alderman Thackray has his name re-gilded at the top of the Ladder, and rides up the fell road some mornings on a grey cob to look at a chimney, and weeps, and rides back, and the price of oak is thirty-one shillings the cord." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Rule fate_thackray_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_thackray) says "The Ladder of Merit is gilded for the year with HUGH THACKRAY, WOOD-REEVE at the top of it, and the price of oak is thirty-one shillings the cord." { Assert spread(fate_thackray). }
  Entity fate_thackray: fact "Thackray".
  Rule fate_widow when accounting() and betrothed(joan) and not spread(fate_widow) says "The banns of Joan Pickersgill, widow, and Abel Lumb, proxy, will be read in the Minster on the first Sunday after the Fast. Abel has eaten every day this week and has stopped being able to see through his hands. Mistress Pickersgill has stopped paying anyone to fast for her thoughts, on the grounds that she means to act on them." { Assert spread(fate_widow). }
  Rule fate_widow_fed when accounting() and abelFed(abel) and not betrothed(joan) and not spread(fate_widow) says "Abel Lumb eats, and does not fast for anybody, and goes past Tanners' Row every day the long way round, and Mistress Pickersgill pays fourteen fasts a week for her thoughts to somebody else, and goes down on Mondays to watch, and comes home cross." { Assert spread(fate_widow). }
  Rule fate_widow_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_widow) says "Abel Lumb fasts for Mistress Pickersgill's thoughts, eleven a week, and she goes down on Mondays to watch him not eat; and neither of them has said anything to anyone." { Assert spread(fate_widow). }
  Entity fate_widow: fact "the widow".
  Rule fate_ladder_exposed when accounting() and ladderExposed(dinsdale) and not spread(fate_ladder) says "Mistress Dinsdale and Master Sowerby are both a rung down the Ladder this year, by order of the Lady Penitentiary, for buying penance in advance; their advances went to the Barefoot Hall, which bought a stove with them." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Rule fate_ladder_walked when accounting() and sowerbyWalked(sowerby) and not spread(fate_ladder) says "Master Sowerby is not gilded second on the Ladder this year, because he did not hire a proxy for Ash Day and so was not clean by the canons in time for the gilding; and he does not seem to mind. He has given a widow her money back for a bolt of black cloth, seven years late, with interest." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Rule fate_ladder_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_ladder) says "The Ladder of Merit is gilded for the year with DINSDALE second and SOWERBY third, or the other way about; the city has stopped being able to tell." { Assert spread(fate_ladder). }
  Entity fate_ladder: fact "the Ladder".
  Rule fate_tower_set when accounting() and courseSet(joby) and not spread(fate_tower) says "The north tower of the Minster of Gaunt has a new course of white stone on it, the first in two hundred and eleven years that stayed, and Joby Thwaite goes up the scaffold every morning to look at it, and comes down, and sets another." { Assert spread(fate_tower). }
  Rule fate_tower_pellow when accounting() and pellowExposed(pellow) and not spread(fate_tower) says "Canon Laverock is no longer Master of the Fabric. He has been given a stall in the Minster to sing in, and sings, very sweetly, and the north tower is in the hands of a committee, which is the next best thing to frost." { Assert spread(fate_tower). }
  Rule fate_tower_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_tower) says "On the north tower Joby Thwaite's masons set a course of white stone today, and tonight the frost will get into it." { Assert spread(fate_tower). }
  Entity fate_tower: fact "the tower".
  Rule fate_row_struck when accounting() and struck(barefoot) and not spread(fate_row) says "The Stand reopened on the Thursday, at the old rates. Nobody in the Row has stopped talking about Ash Day, and nobody in the Middle Town has started." { Assert spread(fate_row). }
  Rule fate_row_wood when accounting() and woodOpened(thackray) and not spread(fate_row) says "The dead-wood right is open in the Bishop's Wood, and every child in the Row is out there with a sledge, and the Barefoot Hall's stove is lit, and on the wall the forty-one pegs have the forty-one names on them, painted, in white." { Assert spread(fate_row). }
  Rule fate_row_sledge when accounting() and rowWarmed(barefoot) and not spread(fate_row) says "The Barefoot Hall's stove is lit, on stolen wood, by right; and the woodmen have been told to watch the Bishop's Wood harder; and the Row is warm for a week." { Assert spread(fate_row). }
  Rule fate_row_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_row) says "In the Row the Barefoot sit in their doorways with their feet in bowls, and the stove in the Hall is not lit." { Assert spread(fate_row). }
  Entity fate_row: fact "the Row".
  Rule fate_hal_taken when accounting() and halTaken(hal) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Metcalfe is in the Consistory gaol, in the warm room, for Fastens' Eve and a ladder, and will be heard after the Fast. Prudence Garth's mother has paid her pains and can buy in the Shambles, and Prudence has not been seen on the Steps since." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Rule fate_hal_out when accounting() and escapedWindow(hern) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Metcalfe came back through the Fell Gate on Ash Day morning without his ladder and has not said where he left it." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Rule fate_pru when accounting() and prudenceTurned(prudence) and not spread(fate_hal) says "Prudence Garth is on the Minster steps on Sundays, listening to whoever is preaching there; her mother is on the Register as a defaulter for a hen, or is not, and either way buys her bread in the Row." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Rule fate_hal_none when accounting() and not spread(fate_hal) says "Hal Metcalfe never came to Gaol Lane with his ladder; and Prudence Garth never had to tell." { Assert spread(fate_hal). }
  Entity fate_hal: fact "Hal".
  Rule fate_tib when accounting() and tibBears(party) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Tib Ackroyd is keeping the seventeen nights of cold hearth you broke at Carth, at a shilling a night, in a room in the Row with the window open; he is on the fourth." { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Rule fate_owing when accounting() and pains(party) > 0 and not putOut(party) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Your tally is still notched. In the Register of Gaunt you owe what you owe, and it will be there when you come back, doubled." { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Rule fate_struck_warm when accounting() and putOut(party) and vigilReleased(carth_vigil) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Your name is struck from the Register of Gaunt. You walked south across the Levels in the dark with a barefoot old man in a new grey coat, and at first light you came up the fell to Carth, where there was smoke going up from the chimney at last; and Annis Scaife opened the door to the pair of you and looked at you both for a long time and said, 'Well, you'd better come in, the both of you, and shut that door, it's cold.'" { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Rule fate_struck when accounting() and putOut(party) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Your name is struck from the Register of Gaunt. You walked south across the Levels in the dark with a barefoot old man in a new grey coat, and at first light you came up the fell to Carth, where no smoke goes up, and knocked; and Annis Scaife opened the door, and looked at the pair of you, and stood aside. There are sixteen nights of the vigil left. You are keeping them, with the Scaifes, in the dark, the whole house in one bed, and Hern telling the child stories about Gaunt that are mostly true. It is going to be a long winter at Carth." { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Rule fate_shriven when accounting() and shriven() and not putOut(party) and not spread(fate_tib) says "Your tally is clean. Gaunt has nothing against you, which in Gaunt is the most anybody ever has." { Assert spread(fate_tib). }
  Entity fate_tib: fact "the shrift".
  Rule fate_fly when accounting() and following(fly, party) and not spread(fate_fly) says "Fly the collie is at your heels, and will not be sent back." { Assert spread(fate_fly). }
  Entity fate_fly: fact "Fly".
  // The account is told, and a watch later the book closes on the ending, so that the morning after comes first.
  Relation accountClosed(group). Measure accountAt(group).
  Rule account_closes when accounting() and not accountClosed(party) { Assert accountClosed(party). Set accountAt(party) to watch(clock). }
  Query bookClosed() means accountClosed(party) and watch(clock) > accountAt(party).

  // ── The endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ending the_fast "The Fast" when bookClosed() and verdictFast(consistory) "The Consistory of Gaunt never sat on the matter of Ninian Hern. On Ash Day the burgesses of the city walked their own penances barefoot through the snow in front of the Row, and the Lady Penitentiary adjourned until the Commerce of Merit should resume, which it did, on the Thursday, at the old rates. Hern was let out of the gaol on Lady Day with no charge against him that anybody could remember. He went back to his room in the Row and sat on the step of the Barefoot Hall with his feet in a bowl. The next morning was cold and clear, and the Stand was full.".
  Ending the_flight "The Flight" when bookClosed() and verdictFlight(consistory) "Ninian Hern was put out of Gaunt in his absence, from a city he had already left. Nobody knows where he went. In the spring a drover coming in by the Fell Gate said there was an old man barefoot on the drovers' road west of Carth Fell, preaching to cattle; but drovers will say anything. The next morning the Stand was full, and the Ladder was gilded, and on the Minster steps, where Hern used to stand, nobody stood.".
  Ending the_recantation "The Recantation" when bookClosed() and verdictRecant(consistory) "Ninian Hern recanted in the Chapter House on Ash Day, and went home to the Row that evening, and slept in his own room with somebody's coat over his feet. The Commerce of Merit stands; the Row eats; the Ladder is gilded. On the morning after, very early, someone saw the Lady Penitentiary in the Row without a mask, at the Barefoot copper, tasting the soup, and adding water.".
  Ending the_bearer "The Bearer" when bookClosed() and verdictBearer(consistory) "On Ash Day the Consistory of Gaunt accepted, for the first time in two hundred and eleven years, that a man's sentence could be borne by another, and put out an innocent person for a guilty one in front of the whole city, and wrote it down. The Commerce of Merit has not fallen; it has only been seen. The next morning, at the Stand, the clerk could not find anyone who would be hired for anything, all morning; by afternoon it was business as usual, and by evening it was not quite.".
  Ending put_out_dead "Put Out" when bookClosed() and putOutDead(hern) "Ninian Hern was put out of Gaunt at dusk on Ash Day in a deal coffin, through the Gate of Ash, and left on the Levels in the snow, struck from the Register. In the night someone came out from the Row with a sledge and took him away, and nobody in Gaunt will say where he is buried, though the children on the ditch know, and sing about it, and get it wrong.".
  Ending put_out "Put Out" when bookClosed() and verdictPutOut(consistory) and not putOutDead(hern) "Ninian Hern was put out of Gaunt at dusk on Ash Day, through the Gate of Ash, into the Levels, in what he stood in, struck from the Register; and the gate was shut and chained and sealed, and the city went in to its supper, which was fish. The next morning the snow had covered whatever footprints there were.".
}
